      "body": "Fixes two checker issues and adds reproducible regression evidence. Head `b648748`; kernel baseline `9fa2c29`. Kept draft: the resource-bounded Arena gate is not green.\n\n### Checker changes\n\n- Replace hash-only universe-substitution memo keys with IDs assigned after full substitution equality. Prepare the ID once per traversal instead of sorting/hashing the mapping at every expression node. Clear expression memos before recycling IDs.\n- Return exit 3 for `TcError::Other` rather than reporting internal/parse errors as proof rejection. Accept/reject/decline remain 0/1/2.\n- Add six cache tests, including forced hash collisions, reset safety, all expression kinds, and shared DAGs; add four CLI verdict tests.\n\nNo proof rules, `CONV_DEPTH`, declaration-name exceptions, default evaluator, main branch, or upstream Arena pin changed. The cache collision test exercises collision handling; it is not a demonstrated false-proof exploit against the old checker.\n\n### Verification\n\n- [Repository CI](https://github.com/sankalpsthakur/kiota/actions/runs/35532668521): passed.\n- [Release tests](https://github.com/sankalpsthakur/kiota/actions/runs/35532668561): passed under both default and `KIOTA_NBE=1`; all 16 Python harness tests passed in both CI jobs.\n- [Same-runner microbenchmark](https://github.com/sankalpsthakur/kiota/actions/runs/35532668537): five alternating baseline/candidate runs. Cold substitution median 214.816 ms -> 62.956 ms for 100 iterations (3.41x faster). Warm-cache median 3.728 ms -> 4.290 ms for 20,000 calls (15% slower). Synthetic substitution wall time only, not full-checker speed or Arena instruction counts. The same job verifies malformed JSON exits 1 on baseline and 3 on candidate.\n\n### Arena gate: known failures remain\n\nDefault mode completed all 189 small tests: 70/70 invalid inputs rejected, 117/119 valid inputs accepted, two allocation failures. This matches the [unchanged-kernel baseline run](https://github.com/sankalpsthakur/kiota/actions/runs/35531839283) under identical test hashes and limits.\n\nFailures: `perf/magma-list-deep-n36` and `perf/magma-list-pair-n21`. Both fail a 1,140,850,704-byte allocation; the deep case reaches approximately 25 million interned nodes. The gate uses a **4 GiB virtual-address-space limit and 120 s/test**, not Arena's official resource limits. It is not evidence these are newly introduced official-Arena failures. Candidate NbE sweep was still running at the last check; no full NbE pass is claimed.\n\nThe runner checkpoints each verdict, logs the active test, isolates evaluator jobs, and preserves source/binary/input artifacts before execution so runner loss cannot erase the baseline. It strips inherited diagnostic cutoffs and treats errors, declines, crashes, and timeouts as failures.\n\nFull Mathlib acceptance, large-corpus resource fixes, and a ranking improvement remain unverified. No upstream pin bump or merge is included.\n\nAI coding assistance was used for this change. Validation above distinguishes executed CI and benchmark results from outstanding work.",
